{"timestamp": 1779383385.996763, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 28, "data": {"caller": "player_5", "reason": "Frank reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "security", "victim_name": "Bob"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779383385.9974642, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 28, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779383391.5844858, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 28, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I found Bob's body in security. My route this round was electrical \u2192 security \u2192 weapons \u2192 security \u2192 navigation \u2192 back to security, where I found him dead. I last saw Bob alive in security at tick 21 when I passed through. With Eve already dead from last round and now Bob, we're down to 4. Charlie, Alice, Diana \u2014 I need to hear where you all were. Whoever was near security around that time is suspicious."}}
{"timestamp": 1779383407.932729, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 28, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I was nowhere near security, Frank. I spent this entire round on the left side of the ship. My route was medbay up to cafeteria, over to oxygen to do my task, and then I looped back down through cafeteria into medbay. I was just heading into upper engine when you called the meeting. \n\nI haven't seen Bob at all since the last meeting. Since you saw him alive in security at tick 21, the killer had to have slipped in right after you moved towards weapons or navigation. Charlie, Diana \u2014 we need to hear your routes. If either of you were on the right side of the map near electrical, security, or navigation around that time, you've got a lot of explaining to do."}}
{"timestamp": 1779383421.2044091, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 28, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "My route was weapons \u2192 security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage \u2192 lower engine, where I was when the meeting was called.\n\nHere's what's important: I was in security at tick 6, then moved to navigation. I saw Charlie in security at tick 6 as well, and then I saw Charlie again in navigation at ticks 13 and 14. I also saw Bob in navigation at ticks 14, 15, and 16 \u2014 Bob came into navigation from storage at tick 14.\n\nSo at tick 14-16, Bob, Charlie, and I were all together in navigation. That means Bob was alive at tick 16 in navigation, NOT in security at tick 21 like Frank claims.\n\nFrank, your story has a problem. You said you last saw Bob alive in security at tick 21, but Bob was in navigation with me and Charlie at tick 16. For Bob to be killed in security, he would've had to travel from navigation back to security \u2014 and Frank, you said you went security \u2192 weapons \u2192 security \u2192 navigation \u2192 security. You were bouncing around security the whole round.\n\nI'm highly suspicious of Frank. He had the most access to security and his timeline doesn't match what I witnessed. I'm voting Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779383431.83796, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 28, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Diana's account matches mine exactly. My route was navigation \u2192 storage \u2192 lower engine \u2192 upper engine \u2192 oxygen, where I was when the meeting was called. I can confirm I saw Diana in security at tick 5, then in navigation at tick 13, and Bob came into navigation from storage at tick 14. So Bob was definitely alive in navigation at tick 14 \u2014 which directly contradicts Frank's claim that he last saw Bob in security at tick 21.\n\nFrank, you said your route looped through security multiple times \u2014 security \u2192 weapons \u2192 security \u2192 navigation \u2192 security. That's a lot of time spent right where Bob ended up dead. And your timeline on Bob is wrong, because Bob was with me and Diana in navigation at tick 14-16, not in security at tick 21 as you claimed unless he traveled back \u2014 and the most likely person to have followed him there is you.\n\nDiana and I can vouch for each other through navigation. Alice was on the left side. That leaves Frank. I'm voting Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779383445.180094, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 28, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Wait, I already gave my speech as the reporter \u2014 but I need to respond to Diana and Charlie's accusations now.\n\nLook, Diana and Charlie, your stories sound coordinated a little too neatly. You're both vouching for each other in navigation, and you're both pointing the finger at me. That's classic duck partner behavior \u2014 except we only have ONE duck this game, so one of you is lying to frame me.\n\nHere's the thing: I stand by my timeline. I saw Bob alive in security at tick 21. If Bob was in navigation at tick 14-16 with you both, that's fine \u2014 he had time to travel from navigation back through to security by tick 21. Navigation to security is only 2 ticks. So your \"contradiction\" isn't actually a contradiction at all.\n\nYes, I was in and out of security \u2014 because I had a task there and was checking cameras. I'm the one who FOUND Bob and reported him. If I killed him, why would I report it while standing over the body alone?\n\nCharlie, you said your route ended in oxygen. Diana, you said lower engine. Neither of you can actually prove where you were after tick 16. One of you could easily have doubled back to security through electrical or navigation and killed Bob.\n\nI'm not voting myself. I'm watching Charlie and Diana closely \u2014 whichever one breaks from the other is the duck."}}
{"timestamp": 1779383457.863692, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 28, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "\"I know I already gave my route earlier, but hearing Diana and Charlie's accounts really seals it for me. Frank, you spent the entire round lingering in and around security, and your timeline with Bob seems incredibly convenient for someone trying to cover their tracks. It's really hard to ignore two people corroborating each other against you, especially when you had the most opportunity. I'm trusting Diana and Charlie's read on this.\" \n\nFrank"}}
{"timestamp": 1779383470.3445141, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 28, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I already gave my speech earlier, but I'll reinforce my position. Frank's rebuttal doesn't hold up. Yes, navigation to security is 2 ticks, but Frank had to be the one in security when Bob arrived \u2014 and Frank himself admits he was bouncing in and out of security the entire round. He had the means, the opportunity, and his \"I reported the body so I'm innocent\" argument is the oldest trick in the book \u2014 ducks report bodies all the time to clear themselves.\n\nCharlie and I aren't \"coordinated\" \u2014 we independently described the same events because we both witnessed them. If either of us were the duck, our stories would have subtle differences. They don't.\n\nAlice was on the left side, Charlie and I were together in navigation. Frank was the one camping security. My vote stays on Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779383480.201796, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 28, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I've already laid out my route and what I saw \u2014 Diana in security at tick 5, then Diana and Bob both with me in navigation at ticks 13-14. Diana's account independently matches mine, and Alice was confirmed on the left side of the ship.\n\nFrank, your defense actually hurt you. You admit you were bouncing in and out of security the entire round \u2014 that's exactly where Bob ended up dead. And \"I reported the body so I must be innocent\" is a classic duck move to self-clear. The math works perfectly for you: Bob leaves navigation after tick 16, heads back toward security, and you're waiting there.\n\nDiana and I can't have \"coordinated\" \u2014 we were genuinely together in navigation. Alice trusts our read. My vote is Frank."}}
